<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex reports Jan crude exports.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex reports Jan crude exports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Tuesday it exported an average of 1.59 million barrels per day (BPD) of crude in January.</p>
<p>The company gave no comparison for January 1996, although did give a breakdown of crudes by type and destinations. The breakdown follows.  </p>
<p>  Maya exports					    962,000 BPD</p>
<p>    To North America				    820,000 BPD</p>
<p>    To Europe					     142,000 BPD</p>
<p>    To Far East						   0 BPD</p>
<p>  Isthmus exports					 170,000 BPD</p>
<p>    To North America				    105,000 BPD</p>
<p>    To Europe						 6,000 BPD</p>
<p>    To Far East					    59,000 BPD</p>
<p>  Olmeca Exports					  458,000 BPD</p>
<p>    To North America				    458,000 BPD</p>
<p>Geographical Distribution</p>
<p>    North America					    87 PCT</p>
<p>    Europe							9 PCT</p>
<p>    Far East						    4 PCT</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
